{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"for f in /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed807260302/11/{1,2,3,4,5}.py; do echo '===== '\\\"\"'$f\"; rg -n \"def main|def generate_input|separator|stripe|template|red\" \"$f\"; done'","aggregated_output":"===== /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed807260302/11/1.py\n135:def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n137:    Push the contents of each closed fence out through the side opposite its red marker.\n141:    - Each frame interior contains at least one small foreground object and exactly one red pixel.\n142:    - The red pixel touches exactly one inner wall of its frame; frames do not overlap and there is enough outside space.\n145:    - For each frame, the red marker's inner-wall side gives the blocked side, so the objects move in the opposite cardinal direction.\n147:    - Clear the frame interior, including the red marker, while keeping the frame border unchanged.\n149:    Key insight: The red pixel is only a direction marker; it is not part of the moving object group.\n405:def generate_input() -> np.ndarray:\n===== /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed807260302/11/2.py\n45:def _find_separator(g: np.ndarray) -> int:\n56:    assert len(solid_cols) == 1, \"expected one full-height separator column\"\n108:def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n109:    \"\"\"Sort colored fragments into matching framed containers and stack them by source height.\n117:    - Clear the entire right area back to the black background while preserving the gray separator and the colored frame borders.\n118:    - Match fragments to containers by shared color.\n120:    - Each fragment keeps its cropped shape, is horizontally centered in the frame interior, and uses the left-biased center when the parity is uneven.\n123:    - Color gives the destination container, but the vertical source coordinate gives the stack order, so the right-side fragments visually settle into their same-colored frames.\n127:    sep_col = _find_separator(g)\n138:        assert len(tops) == len(set(tops)), \"same-colored fragments need unique top rows\"\n340:def generate_input() -> np.ndarray:\n===== /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed807260302/11/3.py\n61:    colored = {\n65:    assert colored, \"expected a colored length legend\"\n85:                if ok and len(set(mapping.values())) == count and expected == colored:\n133:def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n139:    - A corner contains a vertical legend of colored horizontal bars: the first\n158:      the colored width legend before the four geometric rays are painted.\n307:def generate_input() -> np.ndarray:\n===== /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed807260302/11/4.py\n130:def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n136:    - Several single-pixel-thick colored lines span the full width or full height of the grid.\n140:    - Detect every full-width or full-height colored line as a mirror line.\n146:    - The line color serves both as the ownership cue for the nearest-line match and as the color used to draw the mirrored copy.\n367:def generate_input() -> np.ndarray:\n===== /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed807260302/11/5.py\n89:def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n91:    Grow each seed inside its rectangular frame into the largest centered solid square allowed by the nearest inner wall.\n95:    - One or more non-overlapping orange one-pixel hollow rectangular frames are scattered across the grid.\n101:    - Let m be the smallest of those four gaps, then fill the seed's color on the centered square spanning m cells in every cardinal direction from the seed, clipped to the frame interior.\n243:def generate_input() -> np.ndarray:\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
